@vsm 1.0
// EXP-MC-01/results.vsm — Monte-Carlo basin volume — RESULTS
// domain_context: {target=vos_kernel, env=analysis, layer=L+2}
// date: 2026-06-02 | ref: spec.vsm (this dir), EXP-AB-01 (basin_floor)
// status: DONE | binary: basin_mc (main.rs) | run: n02 VSF_MC_SAMPLES=200 seed=42

results(EXP-MC-01, "Monte-Carlo basin volume on the 4-state occupation simplex"):

  setup: "warmup 2000t → attractor (frozen reference); 200 trials, each kick p → q~Dirichlet(1,1,1,1)
          by κ~U(0,0.95] over 10t, then 990t relax + 1000t recovery. deterministic splitmix64 seed=42."

  numbers:
    basin_volume_fraction: "1.0000 (200/200 recovered, final stasis_cos ≥ 0.90)"
    stasis_cos_min:        "overall 0.9452 | p5 0.9724 | mean 0.9915"
    per_band_recovery:     "ALL κ-bands [0,0.2)..[0.8,1.0) = 1.000 recovery"
    delta_safe:            "[0.8,1.0) — even the strongest kicks recover"

  hypotheses:
    H_MC1_volume:    "CONFIRMED — basin_volume_fraction ≈ 1.0. The attractor basin contains the entire
                      reachable simplex perturbation region (direction × magnitude). Consistent with
                      EXP-AB-01 H2-rejected (viable never breached)."
    H_MC2_isotropy:  "CONFIRMED + REFINED — the RANDOM-direction floor (min 0.9452) is HIGHER than
                      EXP-AB-01's single-direction floor 0.875. ⇒ the [1,0,0,0] ground-state kick used by
                      EXP-AB-01 is the WORST-CASE direction (max distance from Boltzmann equilibrium);
                      typical/random directions are gentler. The floor is NOT isotropic — it has a
                      worst-case corner — but is bounded in ALL directions."
    H_MC3_monotone:  "consistent — all bands recover; min decreases toward the worst-case corner only."

  interpretation:
    "EXP-AB-01's basin_floor 0.875 is a CONSERVATIVE worst-case bound (the hardest direction). EXP-MC-01
     upgrades the claim from a 6-point single-direction sweep to a DENSITY estimate: basin volume fraction
     ≈ 1.0 over the reachable perturbation region, typical-direction floor ≈ 0.945. Closes Q7."

  calibration_impact:
    "BASIN_FLOOR = 0.875 stays the conservative (worst-case) constant — now density-BACKED by 2
     experiments (EXP-AB-01 worst-case + EXP-MC-01 volume). RESILIENCE_MARGIN 0.175 is the worst-case
     head-room; random-direction head-room ≈ 0.245. No code value changes; calibration.vsm annotated."

  paper: "attractor_convergence §Basin Geometry — replaces the sparse 6-δ result with a Monte-Carlo
          volume estimate; addresses the 'single direction / hand-picked δ' reviewer objection."

  followup_optional:
    "wider magnitude (κ via larger effective δ) or non-simplex perturbation families could probe whether
     ANY direction breaches viability — but within the reachable simplex, volume is already ≈ 1.0."

